Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The data files of the original program", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"df875a0f-3e69-4d97-83ac-84aef87b2af2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The original program t2_fields wrote the numbers of its two figures into \
three data files: t2_dispersion_lattice.csv (the 48 points of Figure 1: for \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["W",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8656c3-519e-4e9a-b527-69a01f69beaa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["W",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21a3f3a0-7ae9-49c6-b13d-39474fb4af42"],
 " and each of the 24 momenta, the largest eigenvalue of the lattice \
operator), t2_dispersion_curves.csv (the 802 points of the curves of Figure \
1: for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["W",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e54045e-cdf2-4d84-84ed-79b8c03e22c8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["W",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f25c711c-9c50-4534-9acc-3ea2ecb68a85"],
 " and each of 401 momenta, the continuum energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87b86ac3-c6d1-4995-9cc3-48b83d8db18f"],
 " and the formula of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["lat",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa8c786d-030e-4266-90a5-ada8872741f4"],
 ") and t2_cvode_accuracy.csv (the 41 rows of its integrations of GS-13 by \
CVODE: the output time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93f8d7fb-5948-476e-8a51-0dbbc9b1b2ae"],
 "; the relative deviations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["rel",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "054b0b03-1141-40d7-b10e-54e8329fd591"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["tol",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}]], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "12"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec160d81-ace5-4b68-aa4f-0ac1e146739c"],
 "; and, for the same three tolerances, the length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["CV",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4928f167-9a47-4cf5-9820-77d4476ec759"],
 " and the order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["CV",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e3ad73bf-a833-4f6b-97f0-e78961a805b2"],
 " of the last internal step of CVODE before the output time, 0 in the first \
row). The first two files print their numbers with 10 decimals, the third \
with 7 significant digits (its times with 4 decimals). The next cell contains \
every number of the three files, copied without change of a digit (a number \
with an exponent is written in the notation of the Wolfram Language), so that \
the notebook stays complete. It is a closed cell: the notebook evaluates it \
like every other cell, but shows only its thin cell bracket, and a printed \
copy of the notebook leaves it out, so that the notebook does not carry many \
pages of numbers. To read the numbers, select the bracket of the cell and \
choose Cell > Cell Properties > Open. Its output, the next cell that is \
shown, is the list of the numbers of rows of the three lists ",
 StyleBox["t2origPoints",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["t2origCurves",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["t2origCvode",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ". The check after it compares the numbers of Figure 1 with the lists ",
 StyleBox["points",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["curves",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " computed above, row by row and column by column; because the files are \
rounded, deviations up to half a unit of the last printed decimal, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"5", "\[Times]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "11"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9b3165c-7cbb-4fef-8132-6d91f41aded8"],
 ", are expected, and larger deviations would mean that the rewritten \
programs compute different numbers. The integrations by CVODE cannot be \
repeated in the Wolfram Language; for them the check confirms that the file \
has the output times of GS-13 and that its numbers show what the original \
check GS-13 states: the deviations are rounding errors in the first row, stay \
below ",
