Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\"PASS  \"", Bold, 
     RGBColor[0, 
      Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"AS-1: \"", 
    "\"free spinor charges in constant gauge potentials (case A): on a \
periodic chain of 32 sites along x_LL^1 (dx = 0.5, r_W = 1, m = 0.4, mu = \
0.2, g_v = 0.7, g_F = 0.45) with the constant potentials Av_LL^3_1 = 0.8 and \
AF_LL_1 = 0.6 (in the links) and Av_LL^3_0 = 0.5 and AF_LL_0 = 0.3 (in the \
potential matrix), and no pair field, the 16 eigenvalues of the lattice \
operator on the plane wave of each allowed momentum q are, for each isospin \
component (Q_LL = +1/2 with Acal_up_p = g_F AF_LL_p + g_v Av_LL^3_p/2, Q_LL = \
-1/2 with Acal_down_p = g_F AF_LL_p - g_v Av_LL^3_p/2), +-eps_lat(q - Acal_1) \
- Acal_0 - mu (particles) and -(+-eps_lat(q + Acal_1) - Acal_0 - mu) (holes), \
each twice: the potential of the space direction shifts the momentum (minimal \
coupling q -> q - Acal_1) and the potential of the time direction shifts the \
energy; the particle block does not mix the two isospin components, and its \
restriction to each component has the eigenvalues +-eps_lat(q - Acal_1) - \
Acal_0 - mu (tolerance 1e-12)\"", 
    "\"  -- largest deviation 1.5e-14; Acal_up_1 = 0.5500, Acal_down_1 = \
-0.0100, Acal_up_0 = 0.3100, Acal_down_0 = -0.0400 (original: 9.8e-15; \
0.5500, -0.0100, 0.3100, -0.0400)\""},
