Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The data files of the original program", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b6008781-7b3b-40fc-b52d-32249846b26f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The original program t2_analytic wrote the numbers of its figures into \
eleven data files. The next cell contains every number of these files, copied \
without change of a digit. It is a closed cell: the notebook evaluates it \
like every other cell, but shows only its thin cell bracket, and a printed \
copy of the notebook leaves it out, so that the notebook stays complete \
without many pages of numbers. To read the numbers, select the bracket of the \
cell and choose Cell > Cell Properties > Open. Its output, the next cell that \
is shown, is the list of the numbers of rows of the eleven lists. Two changes \
of form were made in the copy: a number with an exponent is written in the \
notation of the Wolfram Language, and a column of words is coded by numbers \
(the branch positive or negative of the curves of case A as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5434d9-ad4c-4e04-8927-319fd937354c"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af9ddae7-da56-4b60-9a66-336b4088930c"],
 "; the source of a value as 0 for a closed form or a formula and 1 for a \
quadrature or a numerical diagonalization)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63f77e44-809a-40bb-9fbb-a02a6d1ce039"],

