Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The figures of item [2]", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2d9e03a8-8207-43ce-94e6-38620736539c"],

Cell["\<\
The Figures 3 to 6 are the figures of the original program, drawn here from \
the rows that this chapter computed (the comments of the cells name the \
lists). The panels of a figure stand one below the other, each with its \
legend, so that no figure is wider than the printed page; the Figures 4 and 5 \
take two cells each. A curve is a formula or an exact solution; a point is a \
result of a computation on the lattice (an eigenvalue, a state of an \
integration, a density). In the two panels with a time integration, Figure \
3(b) and Figure 4(b), the points alternate between the integration by IDA in \
this notebook and the integration by CVODE in the original program, whose \
numbers stand in the data cell above.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e729dde3-1f1f-486b-993a-dcfdc14d8055"],

