Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"check\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"result\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"statement\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"AS-1\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"free spinor charges in constant gauge potentials (case A): \
on a periodic chain of 32 sites along x_LL^1 (dx = 0.5, r_W = 1, m = 0.4, mu \
= 0.2, g_v = 0.7, g_F = 0.45) with the constant potentials Av_LL^3_1 = 0.8 \
and AF_LL_1 = 0.6 (in the links) and Av_LL^3_0 = 0.5 and AF_LL_0 = 0.3 (in \
the potential matrix), and no pair field, the 16 eigenvalues of the lattice \
operator on the plane wave of each allowed momentum q are, for each isospin \
component (Q_LL = +1/2 with Acal_up_p = g_F AF_LL_p + g_v Av_LL^3_p/2, Q_LL = \
-1/2 with Acal_down_p = g_F AF_LL_p - g_v Av_LL^3_p/2), +-eps_lat(q - Acal_1) \
- Acal_0 - mu (particles) and -(+-eps_lat(q + Acal_1) - Acal_0 - mu) (holes), \
each twice: the potential of the space direction shifts the momentum (minimal \
coupling q -> q - Acal_1) and the potential of the time direction shifts the \
energy; the particle block does not mix the two isospin components, and its \
restriction to each component has the eigenvalues +-eps_lat(q - Acal_1) - \
Acal_0 - mu (tolerance 1e-12)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-2\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"isospin precession in a constant isospin potential (case \
A): in the potential Av_LL^1_0 = 1.5 (along tau_1, no other field) the \
positive-energy lattice plane wave chi_pw (x) (isospin up) evolves as exp(-i \
(eps_lat - mu) x_LL^0) chi_pw (x) (cos(omega_pr x_LL^0/2), i sin(omega_pr \
x_LL^0/2)) with omega_pr = g_v Av_LL^1_0, so that P_up = cos^2(omega_pr \
x_LL^0/2); the integration of the lattice equations by IDA (SUNDIALS, through \
NDSolve with Method -> \\\"IDA\\\", in place of CVODE of the original \
program; rtol = 1e-12, atol = 1e-14; periodic chain of 16 sites, dx = 0.5, \
r_W = 1, m = 0.4, mu = 0.2, momentum 2 pi 2/(16 dx)) agrees with this exact \
solution at the 101 output times x_LL^0 = 0, 0.16, ..., 16: (1) the relative \
deviation of the whole state stays below 1e-9, the tolerance of the original \
check; (2) the states at the output times are the cubic Hermite polynomials \
of the stored values and derivatives (tolerance 1e-12), and the largest \
deviation is at most the bound that follows from the measured exact local \
errors of the internal steps, (1 + h_IDA E_max/4) (sum of local_error) + \
h_IDA deriv_residual/4 + (h_IDA E_max)^4/384 (norm of the state); the numbers \
of steps and of evaluations of IDA and the largest ratio \
local_error/budget_step, with budget_step = rtol (norm of the state) + atol \
sqrt(512), are stated\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-3\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the Bogoliubov modes of the uniform polar superfluid dvec = \
(0, 0, Delta) (case B): Kch_3 h(q) = conj(h(-q)) Kch_3, so that for an \
eigenvector chi_pw of h(q) with the energy +eps or -eps the hole vector Kch_3 \
chi_pw is an eigenvector of conj(h(-q)) with the same energy; Ppair = Delta \
Kch_3^dag couples (chi_pw, 0) only to (0, Kch_3 chi_pw), and (cos theta_B \
chi_pw, sin theta_B Kch_3 chi_pw) with cos^2 theta_B = (1 + (+-eps - \
mu)/E)/2, sin^2 theta_B = (1 - (+-eps - mu)/E)/2, E = ((+-eps - mu)^2 + \
Delta^2)^(1/2), is an eigenvector of H_BdG(q) with the energy E, which is E^- \
for the positive branch +eps and E^+ for the negative branch -eps (50 random \
momenta, chemical potentials and gaps, m = 0.4; tolerance 1e-12); on the \
lattice (periodic chain of 32 sites, dx = 0.5, r_W = 1, m = 0.4, mu = 0.6, \
Delta = 0.3) the 16 eigenvalues of the lattice operator on the plane wave of \
each allowed momentum are +-E^- and +-E^+ with eps_lat in place of eps, each \
four times (tolerance 1e-12)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-4\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the particle-hole (Rabi) oscillation of a particle injected \
into the uniform polar superfluid (case B): on a periodic chain of 16 sites \
(dx = 0.5, r_W = 1, m = 0.4, mu = 0.6) with the pair field dvec = (0, 0, \
0.3), the positive-energy lattice plane wave chi_pw of isospin up at the \
momentum 2 pi/(16 dx) evolves as (cos(E^- x_LL^0) - i ((eps_lat - mu)/E^-) \
sin(E^- x_LL^0)) (chi_pw, 0) - i (Delta/E^-) sin(E^- x_LL^0) (0, Kch_3 \
chi_pw), with E^- = ((eps_lat - mu)^2 + Delta^2)^(1/2): the probability of \
the hole is P_hole = (Delta/E^-)^2 sin^2(E^- x_LL^0); the integration of the \
lattice equations by IDA (SUNDIALS, through NDSolve with Method -> \
\\\"IDA\\\", in place of CVODE of the original program; rtol = 1e-12, atol = \
1e-14) agrees with this exact solution at the 101 output times x_LL^0 = 0, \
0.2, ..., 20: (1) the relative deviation of the whole state stays below 1e-9, \
the tolerance of the original check; (2) the states at the output times are \
the cubic Hermite polynomials of the stored values and derivatives (tolerance \
1e-12), and the largest deviation is at most the bound that follows from the \
measured exact local errors of the internal steps, (1 + h_IDA E_max/4) (sum \
of local_error) + h_IDA deriv_residual/4 + (h_IDA E_max)^4/384 (norm of the \
state); the numbers of steps and of evaluations of IDA and the largest ratio \
local_error/budget_step, with budget_step = rtol (norm of the state) + atol \
sqrt(512), are stated\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-5\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the gap equation in closed form for massless spinor charges \
(case B): int_(q<Lambda) d^3q/(2 pi)^3 (1/E^+ + 1/E^-) with E^(+-) = ((q +- \
mu)^2 + Delta^2)^(1/2) equals (1/(4 pi^2)) [(Lambda - 3 mu) E^+(Lambda) + \
(Lambda + 3 mu) E^-(Lambda) + (2 mu^2 - Delta^2) (asinh((Lambda + mu)/Delta) \
+ asinh((Lambda - mu)/Delta))] for six pairs (mu, Delta) (relative deviation \
from composite Gauss-Legendre quadrature with 32 nodes per panel, tolerance \
1e-10); its limit Delta -> 0 at mu = 0 is Lambda^2/(2 pi^2), so that G_crit = \
2 pi^2/Lambda^2 (tolerance 1e-8); the gaps Delta(G) found from the closed \
form by bisection satisfy G int(...) = 1 with the integral computed by \
quadrature (the 11 of the 12 cases mu = 0, 0.3, 0.6 with G/G_crit = 0.6, 1.2, \
1.8, 2.4 that have a gap, tolerance 1e-9); and for mu > 0 and weak coupling \
(G < G_crit) the gap approaches the BCS form Delta = 2 (Lambda^2 - \
mu^2)^(1/2) exp(-3/2) exp(-(pi^2/mu^2) (1/G - 1/G_crit)), the relative \
deviation being smaller than twice the size (Delta^2/(2 mu^2)) ln(1/Delta) of \
the leading correction (mu = 0.3, G/G_crit = 0.3, 0.4, 0.5); Lambda = \
1\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-6\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the uniform polar state is an exact self-consistent \
solution of the lattice mean-field equations (case B): on a periodic chain of \
16 sites (dx = 0.5, r_W = 1, m = 0.4, mu = 0.6) with dvec = (0, 0, 0.3), the \
sum over the 128 positive-energy eigenvectors of the lattice operator (unit \
vectors, with the particle part psi_p and the hole part psi_h) of psi_p^T \
Kch_iota conj(psi_h), computed at every site by the routine of the solvers, \
is 0 for iota = 1, 2 and -2 Delta (1/16) sum_q (1/E^+ + 1/E^-) (eps_lat in \
place of eps, the 16 allowed momenta) for iota = 3 (tolerance 1e-12); with \
Pi_iota = dx^(-1) times this sum (the continuum normalization of a chain) and \
the coupling G given by the lattice gap equation 1/G = (1/(16 dx)) sum_q \
(1/E^+ + 1/E^-), the self-consistency condition d_iota = -(G/2) Pi_iota gives \
back dvec = (0, 0, Delta) on every site (tolerance 1e-12): a fixed point that \
the self-consistent solvers must reproduce\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-7\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the bound states of a domain wall (kink) of the pair field \
(case C), in the continuum: the 8 x 8 matrices (Dirac (x) isospin) satisfy \
(Kch_3^dag)^2 = -1, (Kch_3^dag)^dag = -Kch_3^dag, alpha_LL^1 Kch_3^dag \
alpha_LL^1 = -Kch_3^dag and beta_LL Kch_3^dag alpha_LL^1 = -Kch_3^dag \
alpha_LL^1 beta_LL, and alpha_LL^1 and beta_LL are real (tolerance 1e-13); \
for the kink dvec = (0, 0, Delta(x_LL^1)) with Delta(x_LL^1) = Delta_inf \
tanh(x_LL^1/ell_K) (Delta_inf = 1, ell_K = 1) and mu = 0, the mode psi_p = \
phi_K chi_K, psi_h = i Kch_3^dag alpha_LL^1 phi_K chi_K with phi_K = \
cosh(x_LL^1/ell_K)^(-Delta_inf ell_K) (so that d phi_K/d x_LL^1 = -Delta \
phi_K) and a constant chi_K with beta_LL chi_K = +chi_K or -chi_K satisfies \
the sixteen component equations with the energy +m or -m at 50 random points \
(m = 0.4, random chi_K; tolerance 1e-12)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-8\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the square of the operator and the complete spectrum of the \
bound states of a wall (case C): with mu = 0, no gauge fields, dvec = (0, 0, \
Delta(x_LL^1)) real and the plane wave exp(i (q^2 x_LL^2 + q^3 x_LL^3)) along \
the wall, H_DB^2 = (-d^2/d(x_LL^1)^2 + (q^2)^2 + (q^3)^2 + m^2 + Delta^2) \
1_16 + (d Delta/d x_LL^1) Qmat_K with the constant matrix Qmat_K = [[0, -i \
alpha_LL^1 Kch_3^dag], [-i alpha_LL^1 Kch_3, 0]], which is Hermitian, squares \
to the unit matrix and has the trace 0 (tolerance 1e-13), because alpha_LL^j \
Kch_3^dag = -Kch_3^dag conj(alpha_LL^j) for j = 1, 2, 3 (tolerance 1e-13); \
the identity is checked by applying H_DB twice to a Gaussian times a random \
16-component vector, with exact derivatives, for 50 random kinks Delta = \
Delta_inf tanh(x_LL^1/ell_K), points and momenta (m = 0.4; tolerance 1e-11); \
the bound states of the two scalar operators -d^2/d(x_LL^1)^2 + Delta^2 - d \
Delta/d x_LL^1 (the eigenvalue -1 of Qmat_K) and -d^2/d(x_LL^1)^2 + Delta^2 + \
d Delta/d x_LL^1 (the eigenvalue +1) are those of Poeschl-Teller wells, \
Delta_inf^2 - (Delta_inf - k_K/ell_K)^2 for the integers k_K with 0 <= k_K < \
Delta_inf ell_K (eigenvalue -1) and 1 <= k_K < Delta_inf ell_K (eigenvalue \
+1): finite differences with 4000 and 8001 points on (-20, 20), extrapolated, \
give exactly these bound states, and no others below the threshold \
Delta_inf^2, for Delta_inf ell_K = 1 and 2.5 (ell_K = 1; tolerance 1e-6); \
hence the bound states of the wall have the energies +-(m^2 + (q^2)^2 + \
(q^3)^2 + 2 k_K Delta_inf/ell_K - k_K^2/ell_K^2)^(1/2)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-9\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the bound states of the domain wall on the lattice (case \
C): on a ring of length 24 (60 sites, dx = 0.4, r_W = 1, m = 0.4, mu = 0) \
with the kink-antikink profile Delta(x_LL^1) = tanh(x_LL^1 - 6) tanh(18 - \
x_LL^1), the lattice operator has exactly 16 eigenvalues inside 0.8 times the \
continuum threshold (m^2 + Delta_inf^2)^(1/2), eight positive and eight \
negative (four per wall and sign); with the relative residual r of the \
analytic bound state at dx = 0.4 and the distance delta from its Rayleigh \
quotient E_R to the nearest eigenvalue outside the cluster of the eight \
positive bound states, which lies between the neighbours of the cluster: (1) \
the moduli of the 16 eigenvalues lie within r^2/delta + spread of E_R, where \
spread is the largest minus the smallest of the 16 moduli (the theorem of \
Kato and Temple: one eigenvalue of the cluster lies at most r^2/delta above \
E_R and one at most r^2/delta below); (2) the part of the normalized analytic \
state outside the space of the eight eigenvectors near +m has at most the \
norm r/delta (the theorem of Davis and Kahan); (3) the summed density of the \
eight states near +m agrees with the analytic density of the bound states of \
the two walls at second order in r, 1 - (Bhattacharyya coefficient of the two \
normalized densities) < (1/2) (r/delta)^2 (a requirement of the check on the \
scale of (2), not a theorem; the Bhattacharyya coefficient is the sum over \
the sites of the square root of the product of the two densities, each \
normalized to the sum 1); for the analytic bound state of the kink (chi_K \
with the components 1 and 5 equal to 1/sqrt 2 and the others zero, beta_LL \
chi_K = chi_K) on rings with dx = 0.4, 0.2, 0.1, 0.05 the Rayleigh quotient \
E_R equals the exact lattice formula m + (r_W/(2 dx)) sum (phi_K(s+1) - \
phi_K(s))^2 / sum phi_K(s)^2 (tolerance 1e-12), (E_R - m)/(r_W dx) tends to \
1/6 (within 1 per cent at dx = 0.05, the difference decreasing by a factor \
between 3.5 and 4.5 at each halving of dx: the Wilson term shifts the bound \
state at first order in dx, by r_W dx/6, with a correction of order dx^3), \
and the relative residual decreases at least by the factor 0.6 at each \
halving of dx\"\>"},
    {"\<\"AS-10\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"Landau levels (case D): for one isospin component (Q_LL = \
+1/2 or -1/2) in the constant magnetic fields FF_LL_12 = 1.2 of U(1)_F and \
Fv_LL^3_12 = 1.0 of the third isospin direction (Landau gauge AF_LL_2 = \
FF_LL_12 x_LL^1, Av_LL^3_2 = Fv_LL^3_12 x_LL^1; g_v = 0.7, g_F = 0.45), the \
component feels the magnetic field B_up = g_F FF_LL_12 + g_v Fv_LL^3_12/2 or \
B_down = g_F FF_LL_12 - g_v Fv_LL^3_12/2; the Dirac Hamiltonian alpha_LL^1 \
p_1 + alpha_LL^2 (p_2 - B_up x_LL^1) + beta_LL m at p_2 = p_3 = 0 (and the \
same with B_down), with the momentum operators p_j = -i d_j, diagonalized in \
a basis of 120 oscillator states of the frequency |B_up| (or |B_down|) (the \
states with a weight above 1e-8 on the ten highest oscillator states are \
discarded: for each isospin component they are the 40 states of the levels \
110 to 119, which the check does not use, and the two artefacts of the \
truncation, which have the energies +m and -m and live on the highest \
oscillator state), has the energies +m and -m once each and +-(m^2 + 2 n_L \
|B_up|)^(1/2) (or with |B_down|) twice each for n_L = 1 to 10, and no other \
energy below the level 10 (m = 0.4; tolerance 1e-10)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"T2-DATA-2\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"PASS\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      LineColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 0],
      FontColor->RGBColor[0, 
        Rational[2, 3], 
        0]], "\<\"the numbers of the figures of item [2] agree with the \
eleven data files written by the original program t2_analytic \
(t2_A_dispersion_curves, t2_A_dispersion_lattice, t2_A_precession, \
t2_B_bogoliubov_curves, t2_B_bogoliubov_lattice, t2_B_gap, t2_B_rabi, \
t2_C_kink_convergence, t2_C_kink_profile, t2_C_kink_spectrum, t2_D_landau; \
4725 rows): every column printed with 10 decimals within 5.1e-11, half a unit \
of the last printed decimal; the times within 5.1e-5, G/G_crit within 5.1e-6, \
the relative residual within the fraction 5.1e-7; the charges, branches, \
numbers of levels and of eigenvalues and the sources are equal; the \
probabilities P_up and P_hole of the integrated states, computed here with \
IDA and in the files with CVODE, differ by at most 4 (max_deviation of IDA + \
max_deviation of CVODE) + 5.1e-11, the bound that follows from the relative \
deviations of the two integrations from the exact solution\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Top}}},
